# Route definitions for Hearth — the single source of truth, imported by every
# edge that fronts it: ./Caddyfile (standalone) and the AppGateway (several apps
# sharing one public port).
#
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost: on Windows localhost resolves to ::1 first, and each
# cold connection to an IPv4-only listener would eat a ~20 s IPv6 timeout.
#
# Rules for anything added here:
#   - No matcher-less `handle`. Under the AppGateway the catch-all is the landing
#     page, and one here would swallow the other apps' traffic.
#   - Prefix named matchers with the app (@hearth_*). Under the AppGateway every
#     app's snippet is imported into one site block, and matcher names are scoped.

# Backend API. Binds loopback and is reachable only through here. The prefix is
# app-scoped (/hearth-api) rather than a generic /api because under the
# AppGateway every app's snippet is imported into one site block on one origin,
# and a generic prefix would collide. It is NOT stripped — the backend mounts
# its routes under /hearth-api.
#
# Media streams (/hearth-api/media/raw, /media/transcode, /download/*) go through
# here too. flush_interval -1 streams rather than buffers, so long-lived Range
# connections are not dropped under backpressure — the whole reason the frontend
# is a static SPA with nothing of its own in the byte path.
handle /hearth-api/* {
	reverse_proxy {$HEARTH_BACKEND_UPSTREAM:127.0.0.1:5111} {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}

# Frontend: static assets served directly by Caddy — there is no frontend server
# process any more. A named matcher (app-prefixed, per the gateway's convention)
# covers both bare /hearth and /hearth/*, so a user can type either; it does not
# match /hearth-api, whose path does not begin with "/hearth/". The prefix is
# stripped so paths resolve against web/dist, and any path that is not a real
# file falls back to index.html for the hash-routed SPA. `handle_path` is not
# used because it accepts only one matcher argument.
@hearth_web path /hearth /hearth/*
handle @hearth_web {
	uri strip_prefix /hearth
	root * {$HEARTH_WEB_ROOT:./web/dist}
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}
